            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="0891" n="795" xml:id="pg795"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/3908: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dennis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-10T10:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">October 10,
                                1926—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:40
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>162. Captain Wyman, United States Ship <hi rendition="#italic">Denver</hi>,
                    established neutral zone Corinto this morning at 7 o’clock to continue until
                    three days after peace conference. Transfer took place under most favorable
                    conditions. This is the first time neutral zone at Corinto in history.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dennis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
